---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/WaitlistForm.astro';
---
<Layout title="Fable — Open AI workspace for real work" description="Open-source, local-first AI workspace. Your workspace stays on your machine.">
  
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section id="hero" style="padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Open AI workspace for real work.</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 60ch; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
      Fable is an open-source, local-first AI workspace. Your work stays on your machine. Chat with your codebase, delegate work across files and tools, and maintain absolute control at every step.
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <span class="status preview" style="font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;">Windows preview</span>
      <a href="#waitlist" class="btn" style="width: auto; padding: 0.4rem 1.2rem;">Join the waitlist</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Honest Box Disclaimer -->
  <div class="honest-box" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <strong>Grounded Repository State</strong>
    Fable core runs locally without a hosted cloud account. Unsigned Windows preview builds are available to build from source; packaging for macOS and Linux is not yet complete.
  </div>

  <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); margin-bottom: 3rem;" />

  <!-- What it does now (Product Features) -->
  <section id="product" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
    <h2>What Fable is & does today</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">Fable is designed to bypass cloud intermediaries, providing local agency directly on your machine. The following features are fully implemented in the current repository:</p>
    
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Local-First Architecture</h3>
        <p>Built with Tauri 2 and React. All files, prompts, and settings are stored locally in an encrypted SQLite database on your device. No Fable account is required to use the core application.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Knowledge & Retrieval</h3>
        <p>Import local files and folders (up to 2MB). Includes structural chunking (for Markdown, JSON, CSV, YAML) and hybrid lexical/semantic ranking (reciprocal-rank fusion) for secure local search.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Control & Approvals</h3>
        <p>Exposes granular permission levels (Read Only, Ask Me, Work Freely). The Rust runtime persists exact one-time execution permits and audit logs to prevent unauthorized tool execution.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Local Schedules</h3>
        <p>Create, pause, resume, and manage automated task schedules locally. The scheduler leases due occurrences and executes workflows through your connected API providers when the app is active.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Connectors Matrix Section -->
  <section id="connectors" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
    <h2>Connector Status</h2>
    <p>We are committed to absolute honesty regarding integrations. Every connector operates under one of these statuses:</p>
    
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Integration / Feature</th>
            <th>Status</th>
            <th>Capabilities & Constraints</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Local Files & Folders</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status implemented">Implemented</span></td>
            <td>Full local read/import, chunking, and SQLite cache integration.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Knowledge & Memory</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status implemented">Implemented</span></td>
            <td>Durable SQLite storage with Composite-Key isolation (schema v5).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>BYOK API Providers</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status implemented">Implemented</span></td>
            <td>Bring Your Own Key for OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, xAI, and OpenRouter.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Google Connectors</strong> (Drive, Gmail, Calendar)</td>
            <td><span class="status gated">Functional but gated</span></td>
            <td>Works via local PKCE, but requires user-supplied Google Cloud Console OAuth setup.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Confidential Connectors</strong> (Notion, Slack, Linear)</td>
            <td><span class="status gated">Functional but gated</span></td>
            <td>Local adapters are ready, but require client-side configuration or a deployed auth broker.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>GitHub Integration</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status gated">Functional but gated</span></td>
            <td>Read-only for issues, repositories, and PRs. GitHub writes are currently <span class="status missing">Missing</span>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Browser Automation</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status preview">Preview-only</span></td>
            <td>Runs on synthetic test fixtures; live headless transport is deferred.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Local AI Models</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status missing">Missing</span></td>
            <td>UI labels local models as planned/disabled; no offline execution runtime is included.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Voice Dictation</strong></td>
            <td><span class="status preview">Preview-only</span></td>
            <td>Relies on browser Web Speech API; no native offline speech engine is integrated.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="fine">Connector statuses are audited and matched against <code>docs/product/connectors.md</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Local First Matters -->
  <section id="why-local" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
    <h2>Why local-first matters</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 2px solid var(--copper);">
        <h3>Absolute Data Privacy</h3>
        <p>Your codebase, databases, API calls, and workspace context remain strictly on your own hardware. Your data is never collected or analyzed by Fable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 2px solid var(--copper);">
        <h3>Credential Boundaries</h3>
        <p>Your API keys and OAuth tokens are kept in secure OS credential stores (Windows Credential Manager / macOS Keychain) through Tauri's credential boundaries, never in the cloud.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Waitlist Section -->
  <section id="waitlist" style="margin-bottom: 4rem; scroll-margin-top: 2rem;">
    <h2>Join the Fable Windows preview waitlist</h2>
    <p>Sign up to receive updates and access to the unsigned Windows preview. Joining the waitlist does not create a Fable account and does not guarantee early access.</p>
    
    <div class="honest-box">
      <strong>Waitlist & Data Notice:</strong>
      Waitlist emails are stored separately from any OAuth or connector configurations. Fable's desktop workspace does not require a cloud account.
    </div>

    <WaitlistForm />
  </section>

  <!-- Status / Privacy Note -->
  <section id="status-note" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
    <h2>Legal & Project Status</h2>
    <p class="fine">
      Fable is currently in active development. Unsigned Windows preview builds are available to build from source directly from the repository. Full legal notices can be found in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy (Draft)</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
